<div class="archive-note" role="note">
  <p><strong>Archive.</strong> This is the 2025 thinking, kept on the record as it was published. It is not current positioning.</p>
  <p>
    The conviction behind it still stands: people and companies should keep control of what they know and what they
    create as AI does more of the work. Some of the mechanisms have not held up. Paying individuals for ordinary personal
    data through tokenised data vaults has not produced meaningful, recurring income, and zero knowledge proofs do not
    let a model compute on data it cannot see. Where I now put money is set out in
    <a href="/theses/investing-in-the-harness/">Investing in the Harness</a>, and the wider argument in
    <a href="/theses/agents-of-sovereignty/">Agents of Sovereignty</a> (October 2026).
  </p>
</div>
